 width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Muria</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Muria are a Gondi-speaking Adivasi people of the Bastar region of Chhattisgarh, India.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/muridun"><span class="enc-name">Muridun</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Muridun, 'disciples', were the followers of the Sufi teacher Ibn Qasi in the Algarve in south-western al-Andalus.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/muriq-shpata"><span class="enc-name">Muriq Shpata</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Muriq Shpata was an Albanian ruler of the Despotate of Arta in north-western Greece, succeeding Gjin Bua Shpata in 1399.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/murom"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/murom.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Murom</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Murom is a city in Vladimir Oblast, Russia, on the left bank of the Oka.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/muroma"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/muroma.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Muroma</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Muroma were a Finnic people of the middle Oka basin, mentioned in the Primary Chronicle among the peoples paying tribute to the Rus'.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/murong-bao"><span class="enc-name">Murong Bao</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Murong Bao was the second emperor of the Xianbei state of Later Yan and son of its founder Murong Chui.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/murong-chao"><span class="enc-name">Murong Chao</span><span class="enc-type">Person<